1
00:00:00,008 --> 00:00:04,828
Imagine going to your friend's birthday party. You eat, you gossip, you complain about the friend that's too

2
00:00:04,828 --> 00:00:11,408
loud. Sub sounds normal until you discover that someone's Meta glasses recorded everything and created a highlight reel.

3
00:00:11,408 --> 00:00:16,808
Congratulations. अब आप एक content piece बन गए हैं। Hi, I'm Asma. I like researching stories I find fun.

4
00:00:16,808 --> 00:00:19,328
लेकिन आज की story is kind of scary.

5
00:00:19,328 --> 00:00:26,208
Last week, 404 Media reported on a Meta patent that describes glasses that can recognize people, identify interesting

6
00:00:26,208 --> 00:00:31,468
moments, and automatically create a highlight reel. So weird and unnecessary if you ask me.

7
00:00:31,768 --> 00:00:36,128
खैर, for now, it's only a patent, but this for sure tells us the future that the company is

8
00:00:36,128 --> 00:00:42,688
working towards. लेकिन Meta glasses की privacy का problem did not just start right now. In October 2024, two

9
00:00:42,688 --> 00:00:47,528
Harvard students connected the Meta glasses with facial recognition tools and public databases.

10
00:00:47,528 --> 00:00:53,368
They did this experiment to demonstrate that these glasses were capable of looking at complete strangers and uncovering

11
00:00:53,368 --> 00:00:55,988
their personal information like phone numbers and address.

12
00:00:55,988 --> 00:00:57,328
Doesn't that make you uncomfortable?

13
00:00:57,328 --> 00:01:03,128
फिर in April 2025, we found out that Meta changed the default privacy settings for people who already

14
00:01:03,128 --> 00:01:06,768
owned the glasses. Meta AI with camera was switched on automatically.

15
00:01:06,768 --> 00:01:12,408
इसका मतलब यह है कि whenever someone used certain AI features, then Meta could access all the content

16
00:01:12,408 --> 00:01:13,808
captured through those glasses.

17
00:01:13,808 --> 00:01:17,048
And then there was a second change which involved voice recordings.

18
00:01:17,248 --> 00:01:23,168
TechCrunch reported that conversations that followed the "Hey Meta" command could be stored for up to one year to

19
00:01:23,168 --> 00:01:24,908
help improve Meta's products.

20
00:01:24,908 --> 00:01:29,288
At that time, users reportedly could not simply opt out of that storage.

21
00:01:29,288 --> 00:01:32,588
They had to enter the companion app and delete the recordings manually.

22
00:01:32,788 --> 00:01:35,488
Basically, no such thing as consent with Meta.

23
00:01:35,488 --> 00:01:41,908
फिर March 2026 में, Expedite Investigation ने report किया कि Meta के contractors in Kenya कुछ smart glasses की

24
00:01:41,908 --> 00:01:48,748
footage को review कर रहे थे, and they encountered extremely private material, including people changing clothes, intimate moments,

25
00:01:48,748 --> 00:01:50,408
and visible financial information.

26
00:01:50,408 --> 00:01:55,328
So if you think कि glasses पहनने वाला is safe, then you're wrong, because AI features and accidental

27
00:01:55,388 --> 00:01:57,088
activations are just that scary.

28
00:01:57,088 --> 00:02:01,828
Meta says that a small light will turn on whenever a recording is happening to alert people, but people

29
00:02:01,828 --> 00:02:05,108
who want to use it for the wrong stuff are already finding ways around it.

30
00:02:05,108 --> 00:02:11,028
In July 2026, Meta announced that the camera would stop working if it detected physical tampering with the

31
00:02:11,028 --> 00:02:17,008
light, which means कि privacy feature only became important after people reported it. लेकिन it's still not enough.

32
00:02:17,008 --> 00:02:23,328
Many creators reportedly are still using these glasses to record women during uncomfortable pickup and prank videos.

33
00:02:23,328 --> 00:02:29,488
And although Instagram promised to remove this content, Business Insider still found some content online. It is obviously

34
00:02:29,488 --> 00:02:33,708
a very serious concern, which is why the courts in England, Wales, and New York have put a

35
00:02:33,708 --> 00:02:39,128
ban on the glasses. A German rights group called HateAid has also filed a criminal complaint about it,

36
00:02:39,128 --> 00:02:42,388
which means that the danger is not just theoretical anymore.

37
00:02:42,428 --> 00:02:46,288
अब सवाल यह है कि is the convenience of these glasses worth all of this?

38
00:02:46,288 --> 00:02:49,088
और अगर यह सब चलता रहा, then what is the future going to look like?

